  <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="sum">
    <h2 id="sum">The 30 second version</h2>
    <div><span class="k">Problem</span><p>Someone opens it, sees their own car or their own night guard, and swipes it away. And then nothing. No sign the swipe counted.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">Decision</span><p>Confidence tiers and a visible feedback loop. Every alert carries a way to say “this was wrong”, and every correction gets an answer.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">The one metric that matters</span><p>Repeat false alerts after a flag. If this design works, repeat alerts per camera fall every week.</p></div>
    <div><span class="k">What I learned</span><p>In B2B AI, trust is a UI problem before it’s a model problem.</p></div>
  </section>

